{"id": "21caf183-2ac7-4950-9e2d-952a05521c8d", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a conceptual question I can answer directly without tools. The issue is that AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess only covers S3 permissions, not KMS—since the bucket uses SSE-KMS with a customer-managed key, the role also needs kms:Decrypt permission (and likely kms:DescribeKey) to read the encrypted objects.

I should also mention other things worth checking: the key policy itself needs to allow the role (or delegate to IAM), cross-account setups need grants on both sides, VPC endpoint policies could block KMS/S3 calls if running in a VPC, and SCPs or permission boundaries could be silently blocking access too. Since I can't modify IAM myself, I'll walk through the diagnosis and give them the policy statement to add.

